            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anvesh-Kumar-Rayankula",
                        "email": "anvesh.kumar.rayankula@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Anvesh-Kumar-Rayankula"
                    },
                    "message": ":red_circle: Verdict: Request Changes\n1 High \u00b7 2 Medium \u00b7 2 Low severity issues\n\nWhat the change does\nRefactors Verify LDAP ReadOnly User Cannot Change Local User Password from an inline test to a [Template]-based pattern, adding a second data row to cover the ReadOnly target user role in addition to Administrator. A new keyword Verify LDAP ReadOnly User Cannot Change Password Of Local User With Role handles the full flow.\n\nKey findings\n:red_circle: High \u2014 CI Build Failure Unresolved (Blocking)\nOpenBMC CI returned Verified\u22121 on both PS1 and PS2. George Keishing's \"please fix CI failure\" thread is marked resolved in Gerrit, but Jenkins build #138825 still shows a failure. This must be investigated and a PS3 uploaded before the change can merge.\n:large_yellow_circle: Medium \u2014 Redundant VAR initialization at line 867\n\nVAR  ${status}  ${False}           \u2190 dead code, overwritten immediately\n${status}=  Run Keyword And Return Status\n...  Redfish.Login  ${test_local_user}  ${NEW_PASSWORD}\n\n\nRun Keyword And Return Status always sets ${status} unconditionally \u2014 the VAR line has no effect and misleads readers. Just remove it.\n:large_yellow_circle: Medium \u2014 Broken keyword documentation at lines 834\u2013835\n\"created by user covers Administrator and ReadOnly roles\" is grammatically incorrect. Should read: \"Verify that an LDAP ReadOnly user cannot change the password of a local user, for both Administrator and ReadOnly target roles.\"\n:large_green_circle: Low \u2014 Two minor documentation clarity improvements (test case [Documentation] and template data table header comment)."
                }
            ],
